{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh will say.</b> When he hears that they are turning back." "<b>concerning the children of Israel.</b> Upon the children of Israel. And likewise (verse 14) ״YHWH will fight for you״ — upon you; (Genesis 20:13) ״say of me, he is my brother״ — say concerning me." "<b>They are entangled.</b> Locked in and sunken, and in לע״ז שירי״ר, like ״נִבְכֵי יָם״ (Job 38), ״בְּעֵמֶק הַבָּכְא״ (Psalms 84), ״מִבְכִי נְהָרוֹת״ (Job 28)." "<b>They are entangled</b> — they are trapped in the wilderness, for they do not know how to get out of it or where to go."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {2 "the la'az שירי״ר is Old French esgare / égaré, 'lost, bewildered'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:03.605857905Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}